# CS319 In-Class Activity 05 - Movie Gallery

**Author:** Evan Litzer
**Email:** bubaq@iastate.edu
**Date:** 10/9/25
**Course:** CS319 - Construction of User Interfaces

## Description

A dynamic movie gallery web application that fetches movie data from a JSON file and displays it as interactive Bootstrap cards. Users can toggle the visibility of individual movie cards using checkboxes.

## Features

- Fetches movie data asynchronously from a local JSON file
- Dynamically generates Bootstrap-styled card components for each movie
- Displays movie poster, title, and release year
- Individual visibility toggles for each movie card
- Responsive grid layout (1-4 columns depending on screen size)

## Files

- `bubaq_activity05.html` - Main HTML page with Bootstrap integration
- `bubaq_activity05.js` - JavaScript for fetching data and DOM manipulation
- `movies.json` - Movie data (titles, years, poster URLs)

## Technologies

- HTML5
- JavaScript (ES6+ Fetch API)
- Bootstrap 5.3.3

## Usage

1. Open `bubaq_activity05.html` in a web browser
2. Movie cards will automatically load from the JSON data
3. Use checkboxes to show/hide individual movie cards

**Note:** Due to fetch API usage, this must be served from a web server (not opened directly as a file) to avoid CORS issues.

## Movies Included

- Avengers: Endgame (2019)
- Spider-Man: No Way Home (2021)
- Top Gun: Maverick (2022)
- Oppenheimer (2023)
- Black Panther (2018)
- Parasite (2019)
- F1: The Movie (2025)
- Avatar: Fire & Ash (2025)
